WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.235 --> 00:00:02.073
Space,

00:00:02.073 --> 00:00:03.920
the final frontier…

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.486
Our technology is catching up to Star Trek…

00:00:06.486 --> 00:00:07.765
So can we now

00:00:07.765 --> 00:00:09.522
fly the Enterprise?

00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:11.680
“Shall we begin?”

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.040
No! Today the Enterprise couldn’t do half

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:14.815
what the

00:00:14.815 --> 00:00:16.293
filmmakers imagined.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.840
We have too many rules.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.040
Would you ride your bike without a helmet?

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.280
We’ll get him too

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.540
Buckle up day and night

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:23.980
or you will get caught.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:24.840
By contrast,

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.660
the Enterprise didn’t even have seat belts.

00:00:26.758 --> 00:00:27.417
We’re at the point

00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:29.834
where the Enterprise wouldn’t get off the ground.

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:31.771
Of course it would.

00:00:31.771 --> 00:00:33.589
I would be there.

00:00:33.589 --> 00:00:35.346
William Shatner now mocks me

00:00:35.346 --> 00:00:37.284
for calling for less government.

00:00:37.284 --> 00:00:39.500
And that’s a wonderful principle to have.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.198
Government, stay out of our lives.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:41.860
And yet,

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.480
how do you have too many safety rules?

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.812
You don’t know that that wall isn’t going to fall in,

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.449
and if it fell in, and then

00:00:47.449 --> 00:00:48.208
you said,

00:00:48.208 --> 00:00:50.680
”Why didn’t you make a rule?”

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.840
It’s good there are rules about

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:53.241
cigarette smoking

00:00:53.241 --> 00:00:54.799
It’s bad for you,

00:00:54.799 --> 00:00:56.377
but it could be worse for me

00:00:56.377 --> 00:00:58.973
if I’m breathing in second-hand smoke,

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.800
even on your clothes.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.908
That’s worth a regulation.

00:01:02.908 --> 00:01:04.865
And they regulate it, they tax it,

00:01:04.865 --> 00:01:06.183
but they don’t ban it.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.180
Well, because

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:10.757
people want to smoke.

00:01:10.757 --> 00:01:11.676
Yes!

00:01:12.295 --> 00:01:15.470
And free people want to do all kinds of risky things!

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.028
We ought to be allowed to.

00:01:17.028 --> 00:01:18.107
Tomato soup

00:01:18.307 --> 00:01:20.004
Remember that food producing machine

00:01:20.004 --> 00:01:21.460
on the Enterprise?

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.599
There are 14 varieties of tomato soup available

00:01:23.599 --> 00:01:24.798
from this replicator

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:26.715
You could get whatever you wanted.

00:01:26.715 --> 00:01:28.972
In real life, today’s food police would

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.440
limit your choices.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.040
I would like a large Cola.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.380
Your choice is unavailable.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:36.920
Foie Gras.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.698
Your choice is unavailable.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.276
And when the crew had to go,

00:01:40.276 --> 00:01:42.753
regulators would mandate many choices.

00:01:42.753 --> 00:01:44.890
Does this really need to be a thing?

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.420
And the TSA would make it hard to board.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:48.400
No phasers,

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.800
no tricorders,

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:50.900
if I catch you with the tricorder

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.058
you will not make this transport

00:01:53.058 --> 00:01:53.697
Mr. Scott,

00:01:53.697 --> 00:01:55.175
ready to beam up

00:01:55.175 --> 00:01:56.194
Beam up?

00:01:56.194 --> 00:01:57.891
The transportation department would say

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.500
“that’s too dangerous!”

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.620
I watch government regulate

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:03.500
this and that

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.140
and this.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:04.640
Star Trek would have…

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.380
Well aren’t they trying to do good?

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.060
Aren’t they trying?

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.475
Aren’t these little men,

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.820
who’ve never been on a horse,

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.600
trying to do good

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.900
by limiting

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.180
your broken bones

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:17.200
Your argument

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.100
of no regulations

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:18.940
doesn’t hold water.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:19.900
I didn’t say “no regulations”

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.260
Well then, where do you draw the line?

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.760
Many, many fewer.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.694
I want to be able to drink raw milk

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.640
if I’m stupid enough to try it.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.280
Well, but nobody should be drinking milk.

00:02:29.288 --> 00:02:30.366
No other species

00:02:30.366 --> 00:02:32.340
drinks another species’ milk.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.700
If you do it, you’re going to kill yourself.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:37.600
All kinds of terrible things, like flatulence,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.720
will happen to you.

00:02:39.833 --> 00:02:40.772
“Darkness

00:02:41.571 --> 00:02:42.290
is

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.660
coming”

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.380
Darkness has come.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:47.060
because today even Captain Kirk doesn’t

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.100
want to explore space

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.820
We can’t live on Mars, a)

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:51.836
and b)

00:02:51.836 --> 00:02:53.894
to get three people to Mars

00:02:53.894 --> 00:02:57.988
is monumental in cost,

00:02:57.988 --> 00:03:00.900
so you’re not going to populate Mars,

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.860
you’re going to send some people to die, or get out

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.098
of there as quickly as possible.

00:03:05.098 --> 00:03:06.616
It's going to be like the moon.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.340
Oh come on,

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.840
private space travel is taking over.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.320
NASA no longer insists on government doing it all.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.780
We could be entering a wonderful new era of

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:22.114
libertarian exploration…

00:03:22.114 --> 00:03:24.052
We libertarians would do it differently.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.120
We’ll boldly go where no one’s gone before,

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.500
discover new species,

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.080
and…

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.140
leave them alone.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.280
Space,

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.240
the final frontier.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.000
Our continuing mission

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.340
to seek out new life

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.940
and new civilizations

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.620
and leave them alone.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:42.480
To trade with them

00:03:42.486 --> 00:03:43.305
if they want

00:03:43.305 --> 00:03:43.904
but to mostly

00:03:43.904 --> 00:03:44.603
leave them

00:03:44.603 --> 00:03:45.562
alone.

